  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Define f(X)f(X)f(X) as the largest divisor of XXX other than XXX itself. For example, f(12)=6f(12) = 6f(12)=6 and f(7)=1f(7) = 1f(7)=1.\n\nNote that f(1)f(1)f(1) is defined to be 000.",
    "constraints": [
      "Input Format",
      "The first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.",
      "Each test case consists of a single integer KKK.",
      "Output Format",
      "For each test case, output on a new line, the **sum** of all NNN which satisfy f(N)=Kf(N) = Kf(N)=K.",
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤K≤1062 \\le K \\le 10^62≤K≤106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n3\n18",
        "output": "4\n15\n36",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The only number which has f(N)=2f(N) = 2f(N)=2 is 444.\nTest Case 2 : The only numbers which have f(N)=3f(N) = 3f(N)=3 are 666 and 999. The sum of them is 151515."
      }
    ]
